---
/* The second drawing: one run, from the plan to the record.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Five stations, drawn the same way as FigureLoop — panes, hairlines, mono
   eyebrow labels, arrows that are characters. A column on a phone and a row
   from the site's one breakpoint, which is why every arrow is two glyphs with
   only one ever displayed.

   The two colours in it are status, which is the only job semantic colour has
   on this site: the engine's confirm tick is green, and the word for a gate
   that failed is red. Nothing else is decorated. */
---

<figure class="fig-run">
  <div
    class="flow"
    role="img"
    aria-label="One run: a plan states stages, checkpoints and limits. Sessions run the agent loop under a ceiling; at the ceiling, work rolls over to the next session. Gates — commands with exit codes — check the work; a red gate leaves the checkpoint open for another session. A checkpoint is claimed done by the agent but confirmed by the engine. Everything lands in the record: the store, the tracker, and this site's corpus."
  >
    <div class="station" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="s-label">plan</span>
      <span class="s-note">stages · checkpoints · limits, written before anything runs</span>
    </div>

    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h">→</span><span class="v">↓</span></span>

    <div class="station" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="s-label">session</span>
      <span class="s-note">the loop above, under a ceiling</span>
      <span class="s-branch">at the ceiling it rolls over to the next session</span>
    </div>

    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h">→</span><span class="v">↓</span></span>

    <div class="station" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="s-label">gates</span>
      <span class="s-note">commands with exit codes — nobody asks the agent</span>
      <span class="s-branch"><span class="red">red</span> → the checkpoint stays open; another session takes it</span>
    </div>

    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h">→</span><span class="v">↓</span></span>

    <div class="station" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="s-label">done <span class="ok">✓</span></span>
      <span class="s-note">claimed by the agent, confirmed by the engine</span>
    </div>

    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h">→</span><span class="v">↓</span></span>

    <div class="station" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="s-label">record</span>
      <span class="s-note">store · tracker · the corpus this site is built from</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    A run is the whole journey, across as many sessions as it takes. The plan
    is written first and enforced rather than re-decided; the record is what
    is left when the machine stops.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-run {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .station {
    border: var(--rule);
    background: var(--mantle);
    padding: var(--space-s);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3xs);
  }

  .s-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .s-note {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* The exception path, one step quieter than the note above it — it is the
     part of the drawing most readers meet in their own runs first. */
  .s-branch {
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    color: var(--muted);
    border-block-start: var(--rule);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-3xs);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3xs);
  }

  .ok {
    color: var(--green);
  }

  .red {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  .arrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    color: var(--muted);
    align-self: center;
  }

  .arrow .h {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The site's one breakpoint: the run turns to read left-to-right, the way a
     pipeline is imagined, and the arrows turn with it. */
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .flow {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }

    .station {
      flex: 1 1 0;
    }

    .arrow .h {
      display: inline;
    }

    .arrow .v {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
